      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a solid description. I'm looking at my notes for the whole set, and I'm curious about the word choices you're using for these different zones. \n\nFor the Oakwood Heights estate, you used words like \"storied,\" \"refined,\" and \"tranquil.\" But for the East District and Arts Corridor, you've shifted toward \"rebellious,\" \"vibrant,\" and \"dynamic.\" \n\nIf we were to pitch these to a traditional, old-money investor who might be a bit wary of the \"urban\" or \"changing\" nature of the East District or Arts Corridor, would you suggest we lean more into those \"vibrant/creative\" descriptors, or should we try to use more of that \"refined/stately\" language from the Oakwood description to make those areas sound more stable and respectable?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
